        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Chronic pain, medial greater than lateral, gradually worsening over years of manual work. Worse with kneeling, squatting, stairs, prolonged standing onsite, carrying timber, and ladders. Can walk approximately 200–300 m on flat ground before needing to stop and struggles to kneel for more than a few minutes. Turning down heavier jobs and working shorter days of 4–5 hours rather than 8–10 hours."
